{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And He afflicted you and let you hunger.</b> 'And He afflicted you' on the way, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 102:24): ״ענה בדרך כחי״ — 'He answered me in the way of my strength'; 'and He let you hunger' from physical foods such as the other nations eat." "<b>And He fed you the manna.</b> Which is heavenly bread, not physical." "<b>Which your fathers did not know.</b> It is possible to interpret this of the fathers literally — Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob — and Scripture would be saying: you merited that celebrated miracles were performed for you, such as the fathers did not merit, for their apprehension was not through the power of the particular Name of HaShem, by which celebrated and newly created miracles in nature are performed, but rather through the power of El Shaddai, by which hidden miracles are performed — those that appear to a person as though they come by way of nature. And he said this because the manna was among the celebrated miracles." "<b>Not by bread alone.</b> By way of the bread with which a person is familiar, a person's life-force is not in it alone, without the power that causes it to grow — which is its star (מזלו) and its force; and as our Rabbis of blessed memory said: there is no herb below that does not have a מזל above striking it and saying to it, 'Grow!' — as is said (Job 38:33): ״הידעת חקות שמים אם תשים משטרו בארץ״; and that power that causes growth has another force appointed over it, and that other force has a power of might governing it, sustaining it and maintaining it; and so from force to force, up to the supreme Cause, which is the power of all powers and exalted above all exalted ones, and is the source of life and the life-force of all living things — for behold, Israel for all forty years in the wilderness ate no bread yet lived. This is the meaning of 'by every utterance of the mouth of YHWH does a person live' — that is, by the power decreed from the supernal mouth, in the manner of (Esther 7:8): ״הדבר יצא מפי המלך״ — 'the matter went forth from the mouth of the king,' which means he decreed. And all these intermediary powers Scripture called 'the utterance of the mouth of YHWH,' meaning that they are all decreed and go forth from His power. And this verse comes to inform us that the essence of the life-force is not in nourishment that comes from cause after cause, in the manner of the bread we eat, in which intermediaries abound; rather, the essence of the life-force is in nourishment by the power that draws near to the supreme Cause — for the more a thing draws near to His power, blessed be He, and the more the intermediaries diminish, that is the essence of the life-force. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Exodus 24:11): ״ויחזו את האלהים ויאכלו וישתו״ — Rav Yohanan said: eating is certain, as is said (Proverbs 16:15): ״באור פני מלך חיים״. Rav Yohanan intended to say that the supernal light, which is the life of the soul, its nourishment and its delight, is the certain eating; but nourishment of the body that comes from cause after cause is not certain eating. It appears to me that Scripture called the manna 'the utterance of the mouth of YHWH,' for even though all the intermediaries are all 'the utterance of the mouth of YHWH' — and this is why it says 'every' (כל) — nevertheless the manna was the utterance of the mouth of YHWH literally, from what is written (Exodus 16:4): ״הנני ממטיר לכם לחם מן השמים״ — and understand this. And the meaning of the verse will be: 'For by every utterance of the mouth of YHWH' — which are all the intermediaries — 'does a person live'; how much more so by the utterance of the mouth of YHWH which is the manna, where there is no multiplicity of intermediaries, and it is the utterance of the mouth of YHWH literally — as I have hinted."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:51.986716594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}